# Conventions

- **Hand-written fakes, no mocking library.** There is no `mockito` or
  `mocktail` in this workspace and that is deliberate. Collaborators are small
  interfaces (`SessionStore`, `AuthRepository`), so `implements` is a few lines
  and produces a fake the compiler keeps honest when the interface changes — a
  generated mock just keeps compiling.
- **Exercise the production class over the fake, not a fake of the class.**
  `app/test/fakes/null_session.dart` builds the real `SignOutUseCase` over null
  collaborators; a fake use case would have tested nothing about the wiring.
- Test the behaviour, not the implementation. A test that asserts which private
  method ran fails on every refactor and catches no bugs.
- Cover the failure paths. Every repository returns `Result<T>`; the `Err`
  branch is the one that ships broken.

# Where a test earns its place

- **Interceptors, monitors, and anything with a timer.** Both real bugs found in
  this repo's transport layer were found by tests written after the fact:
  `RetryInterceptor` performed 2 attempts when configured for 3, and
  `ConnectivityMonitorImpl` raised the offline banner ~1.2s *after* the network
  came back. Neither is visible by reading the code.
- **Wiring, routing, theming, startup.** `app/test/app_smoke_test.dart` boots
  the real `Bootstrap.run()` and pumps the real `App`; extend it. The rest of
  the gate has passed on a build that white-screened on the first frame, because
  nothing else in it renders a widget.
- **Every DI module.** `app/test/injection_test.dart` asserts one type per
  external module. A package left out of `externalPackageModulesBefore`
  registers nothing and fails only at runtime.

# Gates

- `make check-deps` fails if a workspace package has no `*_test.dart`, or has
  tests that `TEST_PACKAGES` never runs. A new package arrives with a test.
- `make test-coverage` enforces a workspace threshold **and** a per-package
  floor, so an easy-to-cover pure-Dart package cannot carry an untested one.
- The debt lists — `packagesWithoutTests` in `tools/check_dependencies.dart`,
  `packageExemptions` in `tools/coverage_summary.dart` — are both empty. Adding
  an entry is a decision to record, not a way to make a build pass. Lowering a
  threshold is never the fix.

# Running

```
make test                              # every package
make test PKG=core/core_storage        # one package
make test PKG=app ARGS="--name boots"  # one test
make test-coverage
```
